<title>JAPAN: Japan July raw sugar imports down 6.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan July raw sugar imports down 6.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in July totalled 120,240 tonnes, down by 6.5 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Wednesday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  July 96	June 96	   July 95</p>
<p> Total		  120,240	165,400	   128,591</p>
<p>Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		75,824	104,388	    93,865</p>
<p> Cuba		    10,750	 61,012	     5,353</p>
<p> South Africa	  18,473	    nil		 nil</p>
<p> Australia	     15,193	    nil	    27,858</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first seven months of this year were 860,705 tonnes against 874,783 tonnes during the same period of last year.</p>
</text>
